          "worked_example": "For the helix, differentiate all three coordinates rather than treating z as constant. The horizontal contribution to squared speed is 9(sin²t+cos²t)=9, and the vertical contribution is 16. Thus speed is constantly 5 and length over [0,2] is 10. Divide the derivative by 5 to obtain the unit tangent, with vertical component 0.8. For a plane calculation, use the independent normal (2,−1,2), divide its residual by length 3, and obtain an origin-to-plane distance of 2. The same normalization principle supports both calculations, but tangent and plane normal are different geometric objects.",
